; Tutorial_5_Mark_Filter_and_Sort.inix -- finding a station that may carry the Seahawks game: filter, narrow, order, mark and play.

[about]
Title=5 - Mark, Filter and Sort
Intro=RadioTrail filtered to the stations that mention the Seattle Seahawks, narrowed to Washington, put in order, and one played; then records marked one at a time and in runs.
Setup=DbDo is open; this walk opens RadioTrail.
Homework=Filter RadioTrail for your own team or a favourite genre, then play what is left.

[step]

Say=One want: a station that may be carrying the Seattle Seahawks game, ready to play.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Control plus D, D for DbDo, opens it or brings it forward.
Key=Alt+Control+D
Hear=DbDo
Hear=DbDo ready

[step]

Say=RadioTrail holds the stations. Alt plus Shift plus D, D for Database, opens a template.
Key=Alt+Shift+D
Hear=Template Databases dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I choose RadioTrail and press Enter.
Key=Enter
Hear=(stations, the first station)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus F, F for Filter, shows only the records that match. It begins with a choice, offered as buttons, each with its own letter.
Key=Control+F
Hear=Filter Records dialog
Hear=Any Field button
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Any Field is the first button, so Enter alone presses it; Alt plus F would press Fields instead. It asks for the text to find, wherever it is.
Key=Enter
Hear=Any Field Contains dialog
Hear=Text to find in any field: edit
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I type seahawks and press Enter. Every station that mentions the team anywhere stays: in its name, its tags or its notes, whatever the case.
Key=Enter
Hear=3 records have seahawks.
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Three: a sports station near Seattle, one in British Columbia, and a music station in eastern Washington. Control plus F again; with a filter in force there are more buttons. N for Narrow keeps seahawks and adds a field.
Key=N
Hear=(the field form, a box for each field)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I type Washington in the state box and press Enter.
Key=Enter
Hear=Filter applied. 2 records match.
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Shift plus F says the filter, both parts, in the words each was asked in.
Key=Shift+F
Hear=any field contains seahawks; and where: state = 'Washington'
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus O, O for Order, sorts by a column; I choose the name, and Enter sorts.
Key=Alt+O
Hear=Order Records dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus Shift plus O reverses the order, so KIRO 710 ESPN Seattle, the sports station, comes first.
Key=Alt+Shift+O
Hear=KIRO 710 ESPN Seattle
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus Shift plus P, Play Stream, plays the station I am on in the Homer Player. If the game is on, I hear it.
Key=Alt+Shift+P
Hear=(the Homer Player, playing KIRO)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape closes the player and brings me back to the station.
Key=Escape
Hear=KIRO 710 ESPN Seattle
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus M, M for Mark, marks it, to find it again or act on it later. Control plus Shift plus M would unmark it: Shift reverses.
Key=Control+M
Hear=Marked

[step]

Say=A planned misstep: the filter stays until it is cleared, so a later search finds only these two. Control plus Shift plus F clears it, and I stay on the same station.
Key=Control+Shift+F
Hear=Filter cleared. (the number of stations) records.
Hear=KIRO 710 ESPN Seattle
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Shift plus M asks about marks, changing nothing.
Key=Shift+M
Hear=1 record marked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Shift plus Space reads every marked record in full, to check before acting. Marks are for acting on: Delete, Copy, Export and Play all work on the marked records when there are any.
Key=Shift+Space
Hear=(KIRO's record, field by field)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Marking one at a time is slow for many. F8 drops an anchor at the record I am on.
Key=F8
Hear=Mark anchor

[step]

Say=Down Arrow four records, then Shift plus F8 marks everything from the anchor to here.
Key=Shift+F8
Hear=5 records marked
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus A marks every record, Control plus Shift plus A unmarks them all, and Alt plus Shift plus I swaps marked and unmarked.
Key=Control+Shift+A
Hear=All unmarked

[step]

Say=Shift plus 8 says the order and the filter at once, so I always know what I am looking at.
Key=Shift+8
Hear=Sort: name, descending; Filter: none
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I name the command; the reader gives the key.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Open a template database.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Shift plus D

[step]

Say=Filter, then clear it.
Key=
Hear=Control plus F
Hear=Control plus Shift plus F

[step]

Say=Order by a column, then reverse it.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus O
Hear=Alt plus Shift plus O

[step]

Say=Mark, then unmark.
Key=
Hear=Control plus M
Hear=Control plus Shift plus M

[step]

Say=Play the station.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Shift plus P
